# AerialKit's own settings for this port.
#
# The one thing that cannot be the same on every ESP32 is the network, because
# there is no such thing as "the network" on a chip: a radio is a choice, and a
# build that only has one of them cannot tell you which one is missing.
#
# QEMU has no radio. Its emulated ESP32 has an OpenCores Ethernet MAC, and that
# is the only medium anything on this machine can actually talk over, so it is
# the default and it is the one the automated check uses end to end. A board in
# a field has the other one: an ESP32 devkit has no PHY at all, so the Wi-Fi
# choice is what makes this port work on the aircraft rather than only under
# the emulator.
#
# Wi-Fi credentials live here, in the build configuration, rather than in the
# parameter table. That is partly because the table has no string type and
# partly because it is the right place for a secret: the parameter table is
# served over the config protocol, and a password in it would be readable by
# anything that can reach the aircraft's port. The cost is that changing
# network means rebuilding, which for a field change is a real cost and is
# written down in docs/17-esp32-port.md rather than hidden.

menu "AerialKit"

    choice AK_NET_MEDIUM
        prompt "network medium"
        default AK_NET_OPENETH

        config AK_NET_OPENETH
            bool "OpenCores Ethernet MAC (what QEMU emulates)"
            help
                The medium this repository can test end to end. It exists in
                QEMU's ESP32 model and on almost no real devkit.

        config AK_NET_WIFI
            bool "Wi-Fi"
            help
                What a real board has. Which role the radio plays is not a
                build choice any more: the credentials are parameters
                (wifi_ssid, wifi_pass, wifi_ap_ssid, wifi_mode), so one image
                joins a network, carries one, or decides from what was saved.
                The access point is never open - it needs wifi_pass, because
                the config protocol has no authentication of its own.
    endchoice

endmenu
